    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 090448\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n948 PM PDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n*  Above-normal temperatures expected mid-to-late week.\n\n*  Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts expected across the\n   region Friday through the weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Monday.\nHigh pressure over the southern US will gradually expand and \nstrengthen over the Desert Southwest mid to late week. This will \nresult in rapidly warming temperatures Wednesday and Thursday with\ntemperatures climbing to around 8 to 10 degrees above normal. As \na result, an Extreme Heat Warning has been issued for Thursday for\nDeath Valley, the Las Vegas Valley, Pahrump Valley, Moapa Valley,\nColorado River Valley, southern Mohave County, and southeastern \nSan Bernardino County. Temperatures will begin to trend downward \nstarting Friday as a trough pushes into the western US. This will \nallow temperatures to drop about 5 degrees Friday along with an \nadditional drop around 2 to 4 degrees Saturday with temperatures \nclose to normal by early next week. Generally dry conditions are \nexpected, but some weak monsoonal moisture will be pulled \nnorthward Wednesday and Thursday allowing for at least a slight \nchance of thunderstorms in the Sierra and terrain of the southern \nGreat Basin due to strong daytime heating and weak instability.\n\nThe aforementioned trough pushing into the western US will bring \ncooler temperatures but also bring increasing southwest winds to\nthe region. The strongest winds look to occur Saturday afternoon\nwhere widespread gusts 25-35 MPH are expected, with over a 50% \nchance of gusts over 40 MPH in the western Mojave Desert. There \ncould also be some gusty southerly winds impacting Lake Mohave and\nLake Havasu this weekend, which could impact boaters with winds \nand waves. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill generally follow typical daily directional patterns through \nthe forecast period, with light and variable winds expected to \nshift to the northeast by mid- to late morning, then gradually \nveer to the southwest by mid- to late evening. Wind speeds are \nexpected to remain under 10KT, with VFR conditions prevailing. \nTemperatures Wednesday will exceed 100 degrees between roughly \n20Z-02Z, reaching a high of 105 degrees.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 06Z Forecast Package...Winds will generally\nfollow typical daily directional patterns over the next 24 hours,\nwith speeds around 5-10KT. The primary exception will be along \nthe Lower Colorado River Valley, particularly near KIFP, where \ngusty down-valley northerly winds are expected to develop mid-\nmorning through sunset, with intermittent gusts to around 20-25KT,\nparticularly during the afternoon. VFR conditions will prevail, \nwith passing bands of clouds with bases at or above 12kft. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Gorelow\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
